 @rolux4853  Radeon 7000 series RT is going to be on par with the high end of the NVIDIA 3000 series rt, add the upcoming FSR 3.0 and it should be fine if you get a mid to high tier card. A lot of the benchmarks show 4k Ultra settings with RT - you don't need Ultra settings. Most people can't tell the difference between high and ultra. You just lose 20+ fps. Tweak the settings and you can get RT going with very playable fps.

Ray tracing is in 100 games so far, completely optional, and kills frames on all but the most expensive cards. It's a niche gimmick at this point, looks pretty but isn't worth it for most.

Either developers need to implement RT in more efficient ways or switch to a different system like UE5 Lumen.

